From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: f0xeri <9pik.official@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 04:43:06 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] qwz: reset LMAC ring shadow pointers in qwz_hal_srng_setup()

The head/tail shadow pointers of LMAC rings live in the rdp/wrp host
memory, which qwz_hal_srng_init() clears only at attach and resume. On
a re-init (ifconfig up after the qwz_core_deinit() at the end of
qwz_attach()) they still hold the previous firmware run's values: the
RX refill ring then looked almost full, got ~545 buffers instead of
~4095, and RX starved under load. Zero them when the ring is set up,
as Linux ath12k does in hw_init. The firmware does not use the ring
before HTT ring setup.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sys/dev/ic/qwz.c | 23 ++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sys/dev/ic/qwz.c b/sys/dev/ic/qwz.c
index fc89f709f88857a37bcf8c09a28d1c4e72e23e1b..4b8ac5697e36a7bf78df45f1833db1977a855588 100644
--- a/sys/dev/ic/qwz.c
+++ b/sys/dev/ic/qwz.c
@@ -20125,8 +20125,29 @@ qwz_hal_srng_setup(struct qwz_softc *sc, enum hal_ring_type type,
 		}
 	}
 
-	if (srng_config->mac_type != ATH12K_HAL_SRNG_UMAC)
+	if (srng_config->mac_type != ATH12K_HAL_SRNG_UMAC) {
+#ifdef QWZMAC
+		/*
+		 * QWZMAC: the shadow pointers of LMAC rings live in the
+		 * rdp/wrp memory, which qwz_hal_srng_init() clears only at
+		 * attach and resume. On a re-init (ifconfig up after the
+		 * qwz_core_deinit() at the end of qwz_attach()) they still
+		 * hold the previous firmware run's values: the RX refill
+		 * ring then looked almost full and got ~545 buffers instead
+		 * of ~4095, and RX starved under load. Linux zeroes these in
+		 * hw_init and reallocates the memory on restart. The
+		 * firmware does not use the ring before HTT ring setup.
+		 */
+		if (srng->ring_dir == HAL_SRNG_DIR_SRC) {
+			*srng->u.src_ring.tp_addr = 0;
+			*srng->u.src_ring.hp_addr = 0;
+		} else {
+			*srng->u.dst_ring.hp_addr = 0;
+			*srng->u.dst_ring.tp_addr = 0;
+		}
+#endif
 		return ring_id;
+	}
 
 	qwz_hal_srng_hw_init(sc, srng);
 
